+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`; `data/seed.json` has one key
+per role.
+
+- `viewer`: reads only (`GET`), except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a known key without
+permission answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than `GET` made with a known key writes an audit entry
+`{ at, keyName, method, path, status }`, whatever its outcome (requests
+refused with 401 are not audited). `GET /audit` lists the entries newest
+first and is for managers only.
